{
  "summary": "Encapsulates block and undo file disk flushing and error notification into a private `BlockManager::FlushFile()` helper in `blockstorage.cpp`. Ensures that any flush reporting failure consistently emits a flush-error notification before returning. Adds unit tests in `blockmanager_tests.cpp` to verify that both block and undo flush failures trigger the notification.",
  "problem": "Callers like `FlushStateToDisk()` rely on the invariant that a failed block or undo flush has already emitted a flush-error notification to initiate node shutdown (`AbortNode()`). Previously, this invariant was maintained by manual notification calls in each failure branch inside `FlushBlockFile()` and `FlushUndoFile()`, leaving the risk that future branches or new file flush operations return an error without notifying.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"#35714 makes `FlushStateToDisk()` return `state.Error(...)` when `FlushChainstateBlockFile()` fails, relying on the comment `// FlushChainstateBlockFile() already emitted the flush-error notification.` That invariant holds today, but it is not guaranteed by construction: it depends on every `success = false` branch inside `FlushBlockFile`/`FlushUndoFile` emitting the notification on its own.\""
